<article class="env-remark" id="5C84F9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/5C84F9">Remark <span data-tag="5C84F9">7.3.6.3</span>.</a> Let $p_{\ast }: \calX \rightarrow \calY $ be a cell-like geometric morphism between $\infty $-topoi. Then the unit map $\id _{\calY } \rightarrow p_{\ast } p^{\ast }$ is an equivalence of functors. It follows immediately that $p_{\ast }$ induces an equivalence of shapes $Sh(\calX ) \rightarrow Sh(\calY )$ (see §<a href="/tag/6D6AA0" data-tag="6D6AA0">7.1.6</a>. </p>
</article>